---
title: Policy Matrix
navSection: policies
navFlavorBase: /policies
layout: base.njk
---
{% from "macros.njk" import pdfLink with context %}

<h1>Policy Matrix</h1>
<p class="lede">
  Four policy flavors, each a fixed configuration across four operational dimensions.
  There are four flavors, not sixteen independent combinations: every job is written
  against the same four configurations below.
</p>

<div class="overflow-wrap">
<table class="matrix-table">
<caption class="visually-hidden">Dimension configuration by policy flavor</caption>
<thead>
<tr>
  <th scope="col">Flavor</th>
  <th scope="col">Security</th>
  <th scope="col">Accountability</th>
  <th scope="col">Efficiency</th>
  <th scope="col">Innovation</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
{% for f in policy.flavors %}
<tr>
  <th scope="row">
    <a class="flavor-chip flavor-chip--{{ f.id }}" href="{{ ('/policies/' + f.id + '/index.html') | rel }}">
      <span class="flavor-chip__name">{{ f.name }}: {{ f.label }}</span>
    </a>
  </th>
  {% for dim in ["security", "accountability", "efficiency", "innovation"] %}
  <td><span class="dim-chip dim-chip--{{ f.dimensions[dim] | lower }}">{{ f.dimensions[dim] }}</span></td>
  {% endfor %}
</tr>
{% endfor %}
</tbody>
</table>
</div>

<h2>The four operational dimensions</h2>
<p class="lede">
  County-calibrated definitions. See each flavor's page for which side of Hi/Lo it takes.
</p>
{% for d in policy.dimensions %}
<div class="dimension-def">
  <h3>{{ d.name }}</h3>
  <p class="dimension-def__question">{{ d.operativeQuestion }}</p>
  <div class="hilo-pair">
    <div><h4>Hi</h4><p>{{ d.hi }}</p></div>
    <div><h4>Lo</h4><p>{{ d.lo }}</p></div>
  </div>
</div>
{% endfor %}

{{ pdfLink("compendium", "Download all 16 policy texts and dimension definitions as one PDF") }}
